[17.706,"o","\r\n\u001b[1mwindsor — inspection\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  every number this project quotes, checked against something outside it\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n                                              measured        expected       \r\n\r\n\u001b[1mTHE LINKAGE\u001b[0m\r\n  dV/dtheta against central differences       rel 1.5e-10     < 1.0e-08       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  piston acceleration, likewise               rel 3.4e-10     < 1.0e-08       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  piston travel at BDC is the stroke          rel 0.0e+00     < 1.0e-12       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  V(BDC)/V(TDC) is the compression ratio      rel 0.0e+00     < 1.0e-12       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  eight bores of it come to a 302             301.6 ci        301 to 302      \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mTHE FIRE\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.706,"o","  burn rate integrates to its burn fraction   rel 3.9e-07     < 1.0e-05       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  and that fraction is the stated efficiency  rel 0.0e+00     < 1.0e-06       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  nothing burns before the spark              so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  gamma sags from cold charge to flame        1.246           1.2 to 1.28     \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  sound travels faster in hot exhaust         592.3 m/s       560 to 620      \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mTHE BOTTLENECK\u001b[0m\r\n  stock head at 0.400 in lift, 28in H2O       153.5 cfm       140 to 160      \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mpublished for stock C8OE-F castings: about 150 cfm there\u001b[0m\r\n  and at the cam's own peak lift, 0.426 in    149.9 cfm       135 to 165      \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  effective area peaks and then goes flat     0.195 L/D       0.14 to 0.24    \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  and the factory cam lifts PAST that         0.2403 L/D      at least 0.195  \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m0.426 in on a 1.773 in valve is L/D 0.24, past where the throat\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mstops the curtain growing. a cam is ground for area under the whole\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mcurve, not for the one lift where the head is happiest.\u001b[0m\r\n  blowdown into an atmospheric pipe chokes    so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  flow is signed, so reversion shows          so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mTHE CAMSHAFT, AGAINST THE 1968 CARD\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mthe card gives four events and two durations. the model is built from\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mcentrelines and a separation angle, so all six of these are derived.\u001b[0m\r\n  intake duration, advertised                 rel 0.0e+00     < 1.0e-02       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  exhaust duration, advertised                rel 0.0e+00     < 1.0e-02       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  IVO, before top dead centre                 rel 3.6e-15     < 2.0e-02       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  IVC, after bottom dead centre               rel 0.0e+00     < 2.0e-02       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  EVO, before bottom dead centre              rel 1.1e-15     < 2.0e-02       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  EVC, after top dead centre                  rel 2.4e-15     < 2.0e-02       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  overlap                                     rel 3.6e-15     < 2.0e-02       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2ma card quotes centrelines about the gas-exchange TDC, 360 deg away\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mTHE CARBURETTOR\u001b[0m\r\n  two 1.08 in venturis, area                  11.82 cm2       11 to 12.5      \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  flowing at 3 inHg                           304.8 cfm       270 to 320      \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mAutolite rate the 2100 at 287 cfm; the gap is its discharge\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mcoefficient, which the geometry alone cannot know\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mWHAT WAS NEVER TYPED IN\u001b[0m\r\n  302 firing order, from the forging          1-5-4-2-6-3-7-8 1-5-4-2-6-3-7-8 \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  5.0 H.O., same forging, later cam           1-3-7-2-6-5-4-8 1-3-7-2-6-5-4-8 \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mFord changed the camshaft and nothing else, and so did this\u001b[0m\r\n  the stock forging reads as a cross          cross-plane                     \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  the billet one reads as a line              flat-plane                      \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  the 302 fires every 90 deg                  so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  so does the H.O.                            so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  and so does the flat crank                  so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mnothing at the flywheel can tell the two forgings apart\u001b[0m\r\n  but the right bank hears, cross-plane       180-90-180-270  180-90-180-270  \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  and the right bank hears, flat-plane        180-180-180-180 180-180-180-180 \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  so one of them is lopsided                  so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  and one of them is not                      so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mWHAT IT COST\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.707,"o","  cross-plane secondary force cancels exactly so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.707,"o","  flat-plane secondary force does not         so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.708,"o","  and it is this large                        5000 N          4000 to 6000    \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.708,"o","  tracing a line: no counterweight opposes    1               0.95 to 1       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.709,"o","  cross-plane primary couple traces a circle  0               0 to 0.05       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mTHE ENGINE, RUNNING\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[18.006,"o","  peak cylinder pressure                      63.92 bar       45 to 70        \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  arriving after top dead centre              9.5 deg         8 to 20         \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mtoo early is knock and a hole in a piston; too late is heat out of the pipe\u001b[0m\r\n  exhaust primary pressure swing, low         1.503 bar       0.3 to 3        \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  torque at 3000 rpm                          285.8 lb-ft     250 to 320      \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mFord rated the 1968 302-2V at 210 hp / 4400 and 295 lb-ft / 2400,\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mgross. the model makes 307 at 1985 and 206 at 4994.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mTHE FUEL\u001b[0m\r\n  evaporating petrol chills the charge        23.69 K         20 to 28        \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  past stoich, less of it evaporates in time  so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  flame is quickest just rich of stoich       1.1 phi         1.05 to 1.15    \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  and a lean charge burns slower than stoich  so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mwhich is the whole justification for a vacuum advance\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[18.632,"o","  best torque is rich of stoichiometric       so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mreal engines make best power near 12.5:1, which is phi = 1.18\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mWHAT STOPS THE ENGINE\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.917,"o","  \u001b[2mknock is an index and not a verdict; these are all comparisons\u001b[0m\r\n  worse at low rpm: more time to cook         so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  worse with sixteen more degrees of advance  so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  worse on 87 octane than on 94               so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  worse at 11.5:1 than at 9.5:1               so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.149,"o","  quieter on a rich mixture than on stoich    so                              \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mso compression ratio, advance and octane are one decision, not three\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mWHAT THE PIPES ARE NOT\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mexhaust.hpp models a pipe as two delay lines, which is exact for a\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mLINEAR wave and clamps its source at Mach 1 because a blowdown is not\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mone. riemann.hpp is the nonlinear solver that says what that costs.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.15,"o","  shock tube, against the exact solution      rel 1.0e-05     < 2.0e-03       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  and it invented no mass doing it            rel 1.5e-14     < 1.0e-12       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  and destroyed no energy either              rel 8.0e-15     < 1.0e-12       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.155,"o","  the blowdown front's speed down the pipe    1409 m/s        580 to 2500     \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  which is FASTER than sound ahead of it      137% over                       \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2msound in 900 K exhaust is 586 m/s, and a linear wave travels at exactly\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mthat. this one does not, because it is a shock: its crest is hotter than\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mthe gas ahead and is carried forward by the flow behind, so it outruns\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mits own front. it is why the crack of an exhaust is sharper at the pipe\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mthan it was at the valve, and the engine here cannot reproduce it.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mTHE THESIS\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.356,"o","  \u001b[2mhalf-order energy is the signature of a pulse train that repeats\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mevery two revolutions instead of one. one bank, at idle:\u001b[0m\r\n  cross-plane bank, half-order share          0.701           at least 0.3    \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  flat-plane bank, half-order share           0.001097        0 to 0.1        \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  the cross-plane bank carries far more of it 639x                            \u001b[32mok\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mthat ratio is the entire project, and it came out of four throw angles\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1;32m63 checks, all of them true.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
